      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we will break it down step by step and then combine the results.\n\nFirst, we calculate each term individually:\n\n1. Calculate \\(23^2\\):\n\\[\n23^2 = 23 \\times 23 = 529\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(2(23)(2)\\):\n\\[\n2(23)(2) = 2 \\times 23 \\times 2 = 2 \\times 46 = 92\n\\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(2^2\\):\n\\[\n2^2 = 2 \\times 2 = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we combine these results:\n\\[\n23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2 = 529 + 92 + 4\n\\]\n\nNext, we add these values together:\n\\[\n529 + 92 + 4 = 625\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{625}\\).",
