      "text": "Given $23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2$, we can recognize that this expression fits the form of a binomial square. The binomial square formula is $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$.\n\nHere, $a = 23$ and $b = 2$. Applying the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = (23 + 2)^2 = 23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\n\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate each term:\n\n\\[\n23^2 = 529\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2(23)(2) = 2 \\times 23 \\times 2 = 92\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2^2 = 4\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\n\\[\n529 + 92 + 4 = 625\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the given expression is $\\boxed{625}$.",
