      "text": "To find the value of \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we can recognize that the expression resembles the square of a binomial. Specifically, it matches the form of \\((a + b)^2\\), which is given by \\(a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\).\n\nHere, we can identify:\n\\[a = 23\\]\n\\[b = 2\\]\n\nSo, the expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\) can be rewritten as:\n\\[(23 + 2)^2\\]\n\nNow, we calculate \\(23 + 2\\):\n\\[23 + 2 = 25\\]\n\nNext, we square this result:\n\\[25^2 = 625\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the original expression is:\n\\[\\boxed{625}\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also compute the expression directly:\n\\[23^2 = 529\\]\n\\[2(23)(2) = 92\\]\n\\[2^2 = 4\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\\[529 + 92 + 4 = 625\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the value is indeed \\(\\boxed{625}\\).",
